 comes from us right please  do not sell them an adjustable rate  mortgage you know  and but but you've got to decide we're  in there so there are car dealers that  are you know my cousin's a car dealer  he's a Chevy dealer and he does a great  job I've got several friends here in  Nashville that are car dealers and own  big big companies and you know people in  that business some of them will they'll  loan money to a dead person you know and  finish them off and then other people  are very conservative and careful and  they want the customer to not be harmed  by the transaction so that the customer  comes back to them later and buys their  next car there and if you're that person  I think you're doing that ethically if  you want to be in that business I don't  think everybody that sells cars is evil  you know but I think I think you have to  do it with a matter of I'm going to  treat other people well you know instead  of just making the trains instead just  making the transaction happen to the  detriment of the customer and that's  what you've got to think through and if  you can keep that balance then I don't I  wouldn't yell at you as your friend for  being a car salesman again I don't think  there's anything wrong with selling cars  huh I love car salesmen as a matter of  fact I bought a lot of cars so but you  know and you can make good money selling  cars right now in markets real hot you  make really good money a lot more than  being the receptionist that's for sure  so it's something to look at but if all  they're doing and they want you to make  the sale and you know and turn a blind  eye to what you feel is ethical and what  you feel is proper and what you feel is  uncaring towards people and that kind of  thing then no I wouldn't I wouldn't sell  cars for that organization but there's  other organizations that that you know  are much more reasonable and their  approach to that hey thank you for the  call this is the Dave Ramsey show
 

